    <!-- DACS 2.7 -->
    <bioghist>
      <head>Historical Note</head>
      <p>When Shirley W. Camp moved to Falls Church in 1978, she already had experience as a
        research historian and had published a collection of family stories entitled "Our Parents." </p>
      <p>In Falls Church, Shirley served on the Board of Directors of The Friends of Cherry Hill
        Foundation, was a member of the Falls Church Historical Commission, and in 1987, she began
        to research materials about Cherry Hill Farm.</p>
      <p>In 1997, Shirley W. Camp published the book "Past Times Around Falls Church." In 2009 she
        finished Land Tax Assessments for some Fairfax County, Virginia residents in Falls Church
        and the surrounding area.</p>
    </bioghist>
    <!-- DACS 3.1 -->
    <scopecontent>
      <head>Scope and Content</head>
      <p>The materials include notes and documents related to research.</p>
    </scopecontent>
    <!-- DACS 3.2 -->
    <arrangement>
      <head>Arrangement</head>
      <p>Most documents were organized by subject and chronologically. Series 1 contains documents
        related to the Heritage Symposium. Series 2 contains documents related to Milling and Flour
        Manufacture. Series 3 contains a Land Tax study. Series 4 contains notes related to Falls
        Church residents. Series 5 contains notes. Series 6 contains information about the Civil War
        in Virginia. Series 7 contains floppy disks and slides. </p>
    </arrangement>
    <descgrp type="add">
